// Mutable (not const) because it's overwritten from the "dataFolder"
// setting as soon as the plugin loads (see Dnd2024CharacterSheetPlugin's
// loadSettings/moveDataFolder below) - every ensure*SubFile() helper and
// tracker class reads this module-level binding directly rather than
// threading the setting through every function signature.
let SHARED_FOLDER = "Kompendium/Character Sheet Data";

// Reverse index: main character file path -> that character's companion-
// folder id (see companionFilePath/ensureDataFolderId near
// ConditionsTracker below, and updateDataFolderHiddenCss on the plugin
// class for why the folder is an opaque id rather than the character's
// name). Populated at plugin startup by scanning already-loaded
// frontmatter (cheap - no disk access) and kept current afterward by
// ensureDataFolderId itself plus the vault "rename" handler in onload -
// this is what lets the main-note-deleted cascade in onload() find the
// right companion folder to trash even if Obsidian's metadataCache has
// already dropped that file's frontmatter by the time the "delete" event
// reaches this plugin's own listener (unlike frontmatter, a plain JS Map
// isn't affected by that race).
const dataFolderIdByPath = new Map();

// In-progress ensureDataFolderId() calls, keyed by the main file's path -
// see that function's own comment for why this exists (it closes the
// data_id race that scattered a real character's data across multiple
// orphaned folders during creation).
const dataFolderIdInFlight = new Map();

// Same "module-level binding, synced from settings" pattern as
// SHARED_FOLDER above - user-defined homebrew content (added in Settings >
// D&D 2024 Character Sheet > Homebrew Content) that extends the built-in
// game-data tables (RACE_OPTIONS/RACE_TRAITS, CLASS_OPTIONS/SUBCLASS_MAP)
// so it shows up as real options in the Create Character wizard (and the
// Update Character Sheet wizard's Race/Class/Subclass fields and its
// "+ Add Species Traits"/"+ Insert Homebrew Feature" buttons) without
// editing this file by hand. Synced by syncHomebrewFromSettings(), called
// from loadSettings() and every time a homebrew entry is added/removed in
// the settings tab. "Race" (the base species + its own traits, via the
// Race wizard/homebrewRaces) and "Ancestry" (an optional sub-choice
// attached to a specific race - built-in or homebrew - via the Ancestry
// wizard/homebrewAncestries) are two separate wizards/lists: an Ancestry
// contributes one synthetic trait (see getRaceTraits) to whichever race
// it names, with a "choice" mechanic (Black/Blue/Brass dragon type, Drow/
// High Elf/Wood Elf lineage, etc.) - same idea as the built-in
// RACE_TRAIT_CHOICES table (Draconic Ancestry, Elven Lineage, Fiendish
// Legacy...), just author-defined instead of hardcoded. See
// findRaceSubChoiceTrait/resolveRaceSubChoice for how a homebrew Ancestry
// gets the same "dedicated dropdown right after Race" treatment those
