// ---- Choice-driven features ----
// A handful of named features above (and a few in SUBCLASS_LEVEL_FEATURES)
// don't grant a fixed benefit - they hand the player a list to pick from
// (Weapon Mastery, Fighting Style, Expertise, and so on). Previously the
// Level Up modal just showed these as flat description text with nothing to
// actually choose, so a feature like Weapon Mastery landed on the character
// with no selected weapons. FEATURE_CHOICE_DEFS covers the ones that live
// directly in CLASS_LEVEL_FEATURES above (the common, well-known choices);
// it's matched by feature name (see findFeatureChoiceDef below) wherever the
// Level Up modal is about to display a feature row. Best-effort like the
// rest of this file's built-in game data - this doesn't yet cover every
// choice-feature buried in SUBCLASS_LEVEL_FEATURES's 111 subclasses, just
// the common cross-class ones; add more entries here the same way as those
// come up.
// Fallback only - see getWeaponMasteryOptions below, which builds the real
// option list live from the vault's own weapon notes instead. This stays
// just as a safety net for a vault with no #Item Weapon notes at all yet.
const WEAPON_MASTERY_OPTIONS = [
  "Club", "Dagger", "Greatclub", "Handaxe", "Javelin", "Light Hammer", "Mace",
  "Quarterstaff", "Sickle", "Spear", "Dart", "Shortbow", "Sling",
  "Battleaxe", "Flail", "Glaive", "Greataxe", "Greatsword", "Halberd",
  "Lance", "Longsword", "Maul", "Morningstar", "Pike", "Rapier", "Scimitar",
  "Shortsword", "Trident", "War Pick", "Warhammer", "Whip",
  "Blowgun", "Crossbow, Hand", "Crossbow, Heavy", "Crossbow, Light", "Longbow", "Net",
];
// One-line rules text per 2024 PHB Weapon Mastery property. Extracted
// verbatim from this vault's own generated weapon notes (see
// generate-srd-items.py / the SRD item library's "mastery property" callout
// text), not retyped from memory - so it matches exactly what's already
// written on every weapon note's own stat block. Shown as a hover tooltip
// on the Weapon Mastery picker's chosen options, same treatment as
// FIGHTING_STYLE_DESCRIPTIONS below.
const MASTERY_PROPERTY_DESCRIPTIONS = {
  Cleave: "If you hit a creature with a melee attack roll using this weapon and deal damage to it, you can make an attack roll with the same weapon against a second creature within 5 feet of the first creature that is also within the weapon's reach. On a hit, the second creature takes the weapon's damage, but don't add your ability modifier to that damage unless it's negative. You can use this property only once per turn.",
  Graze: "If you make an attack roll with this weapon against a creature and miss, you can deal damage to that creature equal to the ability modifier used to make the attack roll. This damage is of the same type dealt by the weapon.",
  Nick: "When you take the Attack action and attack with this Light weapon, you can make one of your extra attacks from Two-Weapon Fighting as part of that action instead of as a Bonus Action. You can make this extra attack only once per turn, and if you do, you subtract 1d4 from the damage of the weapon's other attacks this turn.",
  Push: "If you hit a creature with this weapon and deal damage to it, you can push the creature up to 10 feet straight away from yourself if it is Large or smaller.",
  Sap: "If you hit a creature with this weapon and deal damage to it, that creature has Disadvantage on its next attack roll before the start of your next turn.",
  Slow: "If you hit a creature with this weapon and deal damage to it, you can reduce the creature's Speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn. This property doesn't work against a creature that has a Speed of 0.",
  Topple: "If you hit a creature with this weapon and deal damage to it, you can force the creature to make a Constitution saving throw (DC = 8 + your proficiency bonus + the ability modifier used for the attack roll). On a failed save, the creature has the Prone condition.",
  Vex: "If you hit a creature with this weapon and deal damage to it, you can give yourself Advantage on your next attack roll against that creature before the end of your next turn.",
};
// Builds the live "Weapon (Mastery)" option list for the Weapon Mastery
// choice picker straight from the vault's own #Item Weapon notes (the SRD
// item library, plus any homebrew weapon note with its own weapon_mastery
// field) instead of a hardcoded weapon list - a homebrew weapon (even one
// with a non-standard mastery property, like a variant/settings-specific
// weapon) shows up here automatically, and the option text always matches
// whatever's actually on the shelf. Falls back to the static
// WEAPON_MASTERY_OPTIONS list (no mastery shown) if the vault has no
// matching notes yet. `app` may be omitted (falls back immediately) for
// callers that don't have it handy.
function getWeaponMasteryOptions(app) {
  if (!app) return WEAPON_MASTERY_OPTIONS.map((name) => ({ label: name, mastery: "" }));
  const notes = getAllItemNotes(app).filter((n) => n.fm && n.fm.item_category === "Weapon");
  if (notes.length === 0) return WEAPON_MASTERY_OPTIONS.map((name) => ({ label: name, mastery: "" }));
  // Dedup by base weapon NAME (case-insensitive), not by the full "Base
  // (Mastery)" label - a vault with more than one #Item Weapon note for the
  // same weapon (e.g. an older folder layout's notes left in place
  // alongside a newer generated set - see vault-map.md) used to show up as
  // two separate, confusingly different-looking picker options ("Longsword"
  // AND "Longsword (Sap)") whenever the two notes didn't carry identical
  // weapon_mastery data (most often because only one of them had a
  // weapon_mastery field at all). This keeps exactly one entry per base
  // name instead: the first non-blank mastery found for that name wins,
  // and a later duplicate (blank or not) is simply ignored.
  const byBase = new Map();
  for (const { file, fm } of notes) {
    const base = String(fm.item_base || file.basename).trim();
    const key = base.toLowerCase();
    const mastery = String(fm.weapon_mastery || "").trim();
    const existing = byBase.get(key);
    if (!existing || (!existing.mastery && mastery)) byBase.set(key, { base, mastery });
  }
  const results = Array.from(byBase.values()).map(({ base, mastery }) => ({
    label: mastery ? `${base} (${mastery})` : base,
    mastery,
  }));
  results.sort((a, b) => a.label.localeCompare(b.label));
  return results;
}
